<title>ITALY: Italy's Florence sees Sept CPI at 2.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Florence sees Sept CPI at 2.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>FLORENCE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Florence said its September consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Florence's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 2.7 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.08 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0   (0.2)     2.4  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1  (-0.3)     3.9  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.1)     2.2  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.5   (0.6)     3.7  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.6)     2.4  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1   (0.0)     2.3  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.1   (0.4)     1.7  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -1.3   (0.2)     0.2  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.2   (1.1)     2.2  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.5   (0.0)     3.8  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.0)     1.4  (1.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
